sequenceDiagram
    title Execution flow — synchronous REPL and watcher handoff

    participant Main as main.rs REPL orchestration
    participant Input as ReplInput
    participant Sess as CompilerSession
    participant Watcher as FileWatcher

    Note over Main, Watcher: Scope: REPL startup, completed input turns, watcher handoff and shutdown.<br/>Session-call receivers are implicit. signatures are from current source.<br/>Compilation and runtime interiors are owned by their contexts. this diagram adds no facade.<br/>Source: main.rs run_repl/repl_prologue/repl_read_eval_loop and session_v4/lifecycle.rs.

    Main ->> Sess: CompilerSession::new(settings: SessionSettings, project_root: PathBuf, entry_module_name: &str) -> Result<CompilerSession, CranelispError>
    Note over Main, Sess: A construction error exits through the ordinary error path.<br/>The remaining flow assumes a constructed session.
    Main ->> Sess: register_module(module_name: &str) -> Result<(), CranelispError>
    alt initial registration succeeds
        Main ->> Sess: wait_inmem_complete() -> Result<(), SchedulerError>
    end
    opt registration or startup wait fails
        Main ->> Sess: recover_startup_failure(module_name: &str) -> Option<String>
        Note over Sess: Preserve successful forms and report failed forms. the repair REPL remains available.
    end
    Main ->> Sess: mark_entry_eval_owned()
    Main ->> Sess: init_watcher()
    Note over Main, Sess: Prologue also arms the importable index, configures the optional agent,<br/>and prints startup feedback and the banner.
    Note over Watcher: OS callbacks capture file-change events into a channel.<br/>They do not reload modules or publish compiler state.

    loop until EOF or CommandResult::Quit
        Main ->> Sess: prompt_string(compile_ms: u64, eval_ms: u64) -> String
        Note over Main, Input: An incomplete source form uses continuation_prompt_string instead.<br/>Slash commands occupy one line. Search completion notices occur before the prompt.
        Main ->> Input: read_line(prompt: &str, stdout: &mut impl Write) -> ReadOutcome
        Note over Input, Watcher: TTY editing and piped input share ReplInput.<br/>While reading or accumulating a form, watcher events remain queued.<br/>There is no background watcher processor or input-active publication switch.
        Input -->> Main: ReadOutcome::Line(String) or ReadOutcome::Eof
        Note over Main: EOF exits the loop. Incomplete forms return to the continuation read.<br/>The following branches receive one complete input.

        alt optional agent route selected
            Main ->> Sess: agent_turn(text: &str, stdout: &mut impl Write, consent: &mut dyn ConsentReader)
            Note over Main, Sess: Agent consent uses the same input reader.<br/>Tool evaluation uses the ordinary session compiler. no second pipeline.
        else ordinary source or command
            Main ->> Sess: process_commands(src: &str, stdout: &mut impl Write) -> CommandResult
            Sess -->> Main: Nothing, Quit, Final(String), or Compile(String)
            Note over Main: Quit exits before watcher polling. Nothing requires no output.<br/>Final text is rendered through pretty_print.
            opt CommandResult::Compile
                Main ->> Sess: eval(source: &str) -> Result<Option<EvalResult>, CranelispError>
                Note over Sess: Source-ordered macro checkpoints publish independently.<br/>Non-macro forms share their HM cluster and ordinary staged publication.<br/>Successful earlier macro checkpoints survive a later failure.<br/>Executable retention and result disposal follow the existing result-owner contract.
                alt displayable result
                    Main ->> Sess: format_eval_result(result: &EvalResult) -> String
                    Note over Main: Append any cascade report, release the owned program result,<br/>then render the captured text. Record the same feedback for the optional agent.
                    Main ->> Sess: pretty_print(form: &str, stdout: &mut impl Write)
                    opt result is defining
                        Main ->> Sess: regenerate_backing_file()
                    end
                else structural change without displayable result
                    Main ->> Sess: regenerate_backing_file()
                else evaluation error
                    Note over Main: Render the diagnostic. keep the session available for the next turn.
                end
            end
        end

        Main ->> Sess: sync_watcher()
        Main ->> Sess: poll_and_reload() -> Vec<String>
        Note over Sess, Watcher: The REPL thread drains captured events at this completed-turn boundary.<br/>Each reload queues internal scheduler work and waits for compilation to finish.<br/>The next prompt follows reload completion. no public asynchronous re-registration wrapper is needed.<br/>The same poll sequence follows an agent turn.
        Sess -->> Main: reload notifications
        Note over Main: Render notifications, then begin the next prompt.
    end

    Note over Main: Save input history and handle any incomplete EOF form through the ordinary eval path.
    Main ->> Sess: flush_final_persist()
    Main ->> Sess: wait_object_complete() -> Result<(), SchedulerError>
    Main ->> Sess: shutdown()
    Note over Main, Sess: Drain worker activity before session teardown.<br/>Executable and value owners retain their existing lifetime obligations.
